{"seq":372,"elapsed_ms":4053,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"We need answer exactly one complete DUT between [BEGIN] and [DONE]. Need implement TopModule Moore FSM two states. Need no explanation. Let's craft SystemVerilog. Spec: reset active-high synchronous to OFF. Inputs j,k. Output out. OFF out=0, if j=0 stay OFF, j=1 to ON. ON out=1, if k=0 stay ON, k=1 to OFF. Note j only affects OFF, k only ON. Implement.\n\nNeed decide parameter state encoding. Ensure synchronous reset. Output combinational from state or reg? Moore output. Use always_ff @(posedge clk) if (reset) state <= OFF; else case... always_comb out = (state==ON). Use logic.\n\nPotential issue: If both j,k irrelevant in other state. Good.\n\nReturn [BEGIN] ... [DONE]."}}}
{"seq":373,"elapsed_ms":4054,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"[BEGIN]\nmodule TopModule (\n    input  logic clk,\n    input  logic reset,\n    input  logic j,\n    input  logic k,\n    output logic out\n);\n\n    typedef enum logic {\n        OFF = 1'b0,\n        ON  = 1'b1\n    } state_t;\n\n    state_t state, next_state;\n\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (reset)\n            state <= OFF;\n        else\n            state <= next_state;\n    end\n\n    always_comb begin\n        next_state = state;\n        case (state)\n            OFF: next_state = j ? ON : OFF;\n            ON:  next_state = k ? OFF : ON;\n            default: next_state = OFF;\n        endcase\n    end\n\n    always_comb begin\n        out = (state == ON);\n    end\n\nendmodule\n[DONE]"}}}
